@@ -83,6 +83,8 @@ With **Send Avatar References** on for images, **Reference pictures go to** pick
 
 The prompt writer is the way around image models that drop reference pictures, such as NovelAI V5. It needs a writer model that reads images. If the writer refuses them, its request is sent again without the pictures, and that writer gets none until the server restarts. A writer whose connection is marked as not reading images gets none. Sending pictures to the writer costs tokens on every run. Up to four pictures go: the cards named in `[illustrate: characters="…"]`, or else the chat's active characters and persona. **What to carry over from the pictures** says what the writer copies, such as only the look and not the art style. A Roleplay chat can set its own **Reference pictures go to** under **Send Avatar References**.
 
+In a Roleplay chat, the pictures in a lorebook entry's **Reference images** go to the image model too, when the entry is active for the reply. Use them for a costume, a prop or a room the picture should match. No setting turns them on. Only an image service that accepts reference pictures gets them. Stability AI, Arli AI, SD Web UI and Draw Things get none, because they would start the picture from the entry's picture. With **Send Avatar References** on, **Prompt writer** keeps them back too. They come after the [World Maps](../agents/hierarchical-maps.md) **Location reference image** and the avatars, with no more than six pictures in all. An entry with **Position** set to **Outlet** sends its pictures only when its Outlet is used, and never from the Gallery's **Illustrate** button.
+
 ## Control how often it draws
 
 The Illustrator card has an **Open Setup** button for the full setup screen. There you set the default run interval and give it its own image model.
@@ -128,7 +130,8 @@ Illustrator also paints backgrounds. On the Illustrator card in **Chat Settings
 
 - **Generate Scene Backgrounds** paints a background when the story reaches a new place, unless you already have a picture for it.
 - **Weather Versions of Backgrounds** repaints the current background in the story's weather, with the moving rain or snow drawn only on the room's windows.
-- **Decision Model Checks** has a Decision model check every reply for a new place or new weather, so backgrounds don't wait for the run interval.
+- **Time of Day Versions of Backgrounds** repaints the current background at dawn, day, sunset or night when the story's time of day changes.
+- **Decision Model Checks** has a Decision model check every reply for a new place, new weather or a new time of day, so backgrounds don't wait for the run interval.
 
 All three are off by default. See [Backgrounds Made by Illustrator](scene-backgrounds.md).
 
